# Statuses on a tick clock.
#
# Every one of these ends because something says `for <n>s`, or because another line removes it.
# A `stacking duration` status ticks down on its host's `turn_end`, and there is no turn_end in a
# real-time game, so one here would sit on its host for ever -- which is why `stacking duration`,
# `stacking refresh` and `decay ... on turn_end` are error CT337 under `clock ticks`. FINDINGS #14.

# The keepers' shield. `stacking none` so a second Bulwark does not stack the reduction, only
# refreshes how long it lasts.
status "Braced"
  tags buff
  stacking none
  modify damage_taken of owner: -3

# Burning. The status carries the ticking, which is the real-time shape of a damage-over-time:
# the ability that applies it is over the moment it is used, and the burn keeps its own time.
status "Scorched"
  tags debuff, fire
  stacking intensity
  on every 1s:
    deal stacks to owner, ignore block

# What a Signal Flare leaves on a thing: it takes more from everything while it is lit.
status "Lit"
  tags debuff
  stacking none
  modify damage_taken of owner: +3

# A hollow that has been hauled back is off balance and cannot close for a moment. Its own
# advance listener reads this.
status "Reeling"
  tags debuff, control
  stacking none
